Subject: Cantor Shared Attention Tool Adapter P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 7ce01431-3267-4fb1-9f55-2345eb372775
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Shared_Attention_Tool_Adapter_P0.sop

& [Problem] is the verified shared-attention runtime has a JSON process shell but no single reusable typed dispatch or native tool-discovery surface for an inference host

& [Decision] is a shared pure request-response contract plus one stateless MCP adapter
  + CLI and MCP delegate to the same dispatch so transport cannot silently redefine semantic results
  + generated schemas make the full operation surface discoverable without a hand-maintained second type system
  + each call carries complete state so reentry remains inspectable and process-independent

& [RejectedAlternative] is modifying llama.cpp first
  + an ordinary tool loop already tests the intended between-pass semantic reflection and preserves provider portability

& [RejectedAlternative] is storing current frames inside the MCP server
  + hidden mutable server state would complicate replay identity concurrency recovery and caller understanding before the stateless contract is proven

& [RejectedAlternative] is adding operations to existing query_sop or route_attention
  + signed semantic retrieval learned routing and shared-frame transition have different authority and state identities

& [Value] is immediate callable leverage
  + Codex llama.cpp Ollama or a custom controller can integrate the same pure operation without core change
  + later session storage streaming transport or multi-model orchestration can wrap one stable tool contract

& [CostBoundary] is accepted
  + complete frame payloads can be large and generated schemas are correspondingly rich
  + P0 proves protocol equivalence and not provider usefulness latency or semantic-quality improvement
